      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"lynkfox\"]\n\nhan. duh.\n\nand ive heard rumor that george lucas was once spotted wearing a Han Shot First shirt on set ...\n\n[/quote]\n\nHe was, at one point.&nbsp; The story goes that the 2003 Special Edition had to be re-rated because it had changed so much from the original, and that caused some problems.&nbsp; When Star Wars came out, there was no PG-13 rating, only G PG and R.&nbsp; PG was somewhere in between PG and modern PG-13, while G was for any clean movie, not just kiddie fare.&nbsp; In order to keep the PG rating under the new system, some changes had to be made to make it more acceptable to younger audiences.&nbsp; Apparently Lucas wasn&#39;t too happy about it... but he still did it, and he&#39;s said repeatedly that the Special Editions are the only versions of the films that he wants preserved.&nbsp; It&#39;s not just that he wants additional director&#39;s cuts to be added to the films&#39; history, he actually wants to get rid of the theatrical versions entirely.&nbsp; So one photo of him wearing a t-shirt doesn&#39;t help much.\n\nThis is all irrelevant, though, since everyone knows <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KQyd9tEDhSc\">Alderaan</a> shot first.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n",
